course: dictionary
lesson: 14442
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but do different jobs in a sentence. Paling is a noun when it names a thing, and it is a verb form when it shows an action. Look at the words around it to see which job it has. «Dad painted the old wooden palings white.» Here palings are the pointed stakes of a fence, so paling is a thing.
explain: «The sky was paling as the sun went down.» Now paling is an action: the sky was becoming less bright. The clue is the sky, which cannot be a fence. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or is something happening? Then swap in a meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: A paling is one stake, and a set of them joined together is also called palings. Many old gardens had a paling fence, a fence built from many of these stakes side by side. Some people still build paling fences today, so the word is part of everyday life, not just old stories.
fact: A paling is a pointed wooden stake that is part of a fence.
fact: A paling fence is a fence made of many wooden palings.
fact: Paling can also be the -ing form of the verb pale, which means to become pale or less bright.
fact: «The sky was paling» means the sky was becoming less bright, as the sun went down.
fact: When a word can be a noun or a verb, the words around it tell you which job it is doing.
exercise: «Dad painted every wooden paling on the garden fence white.» What is a paling? | A kind of flower | A gate that opens both ways | A bright light in the sky | *A pointed wooden stake that is part of a fence
exercise: «The sky was paling as the sun went down.» What does paling mean here? | *Becoming less bright | Growing taller | Becoming louder | Turning into a fence
exercise: «The cat sat on the lawn, beside the tall palings.» Find and copy the word that names a wooden stake in a fence. | sky | *palings | lawn | cat
test: Mia's family has a paling fence around the garden. What is a paling fence? | A wall made of bricks | *A fence made of wooden stakes | A row of tall trees | A bridge over a stream
test: «Light was paling in the west as the boat sailed home.» What is happening to the light? | *It is becoming less bright | It is moving very fast | It is turning into wood | It is getting brighter
exam: Sam says paling only means becoming pale. Which answer is correct? | *Paling is a noun for a wooden stake or a fence, and also the -ing form of pale | Paling is a colour like grey | Paling only means a wooden stake, never anything else | Paling means a fence and nothing more
